# Aggressive Nmap Scan PCAP

## Overview

This packet capture contains network traffic generated during an aggressive Nmap port scanning attack performed from the Kali Linux attacker machine against the Ubuntu target system.

## Attack Details

- **Attack Type:** Aggressive TCP Port Scan
- **Tool Used:** Nmap
- **Attacker Machine:** Kali Linux
- **Target Machine:** Ubuntu
- **Capture Tool:** tcpdump

## File

- `aggressive_nmap_scan.pcap`

## Analysis

The PCAP was analyzed using Wireshark to investigate reconnaissance activity. Multiple TCP SYN packets targeting different destination ports were observed, indicating an aggressive port scan.

### Wireshark Filters Used

```text
tcp.flags.syn == 1
```

```text
ip.addr == 192.168.111.130
```

*(Replace the IP if your attacker IP is different.)*

## Evidence Collected

- Multiple SYN packets
- Sequential probing of destination ports
- High connection rate from a single source host

## Learning Outcome

This packet capture demonstrates how reconnaissance activity appears at the packet level and how Wireshark can be used to identify TCP SYN port scanning behavior.
